            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0276" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg176"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.1211/256</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Confidential Agent of the Provisional Government
                        of Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Díaz</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Chief of the Division of Mexican Affairs, Department of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnston</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July 2,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Highly Esteemed Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform
                    you that in compliance with instructions from Señor don Adolfo de la Huerta,
                    Acting Constitutional President of the Mexican Republic, I turned over the
                    Embassy on this day to Señor don Fernando Iglesias Calderón, High Commissioner
                    of my Government, with the rank of Ambassador Extraordinary and
                    Plenipotentiary.</p>
                <p>I gladly avail myself of this opportunity to tender you my thanks for the kind
                    attentions shown me while I had charge of the interests of my country at this
                    capital and more particularly for the spirit of cordiality in which you were
                    pleased to attend to all the matters which I have had to bring before the
                    Division in your charge in connection with my official duties.</p>
                <p>I take [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvaro Torre Díaz</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
